## SEV-3 — Structural gaps

### DEF-43 — CAST Vrassik entry named the wrong mek — RESOLVED 2026-09-01

Vrassik’s B1.CH11 line said “consistent with Vekk not matching to him until Book 2.” Vekk is Bruvald’s mek. Vrassik’s is Perrin Cato, already locked on the same sheet as “matched Book 1,” which in turn disagreed with delivered prose (B1.CH11, CH14, CH15 all show him working his rig alone, no mek). **Author ruling: Cato is the mek.** CAST v16 fixes the name and reconciles the timing: matched Book 1, not day one, somewhere after B1.CH16, exact chapter still author-lane. Path Audit §1.3 stays open until that chapter is picked. **Lane:** Author, exercised. **Closed.**

### DEF-42 — B1.CH15 internal timeline off by months — RESOLVED 2026-09-01

Delivered Ch.15 v1 said “six months” since the January rain loophole (Ch.13 dates itself at four), “five weeks back” for Denic’s Ch.9 question (February, so nearer ten), “two months” for Ilyen’s checking since the second week (nearer three), and had Reqa place the same checking “since February.” Found during the Ch.16 LOAD, neighbour read. **Fixed in Ch.15 v2:** four months, “back in February,” three months, “since the second week.” **Lane:** Claude, mechanical. **Closed.**

**Reopened same day, second pass, RESOLVED 2026-09-01.** v2’s own fix left the rain-loophole line dated “back in January,” never checked against Ch.13’s own locked callback (“You did wet in February… I survived wet in February”), the actual origin of the same running bit. Caught by the author, not by LINT, a real miss, the month itself is exactly the kind of concrete detail LINT’s arithmetic check should have flagged and didn’t, since it only checks distances, not the anchor date they’re measured from. **Fixed in Ch.15 v3:** “back in February,” elapsed distance recomputed against Ch.13’s own April placement (Act 2 opens Ch.13) rather than reused from the first pass, two months, not four. **Process note, worth keeping:** Stage 6’s arithmetic check needs a companion step, verify the anchor date itself against every other locked reference to the same event before trusting the distance math built on top of it. **Lane:** Claude, mechanical, author caught it. **Closed.**

### DEF-41 — B1.CH15 delivered H as “the Twelfth Pattern,” contradicting RUNE twice — RESOLVED 2026-09-01

RUNE’s Literacy timeline (DEF-31) locks R and H to early Act 3. Ch.15 v1 delivered H in Act 2. Separately, the “Twelfth” count cannot be right, Ch.13 had already delivered nine letters past the Foundational Nine. **Author ruling: Ch.15 is wrong, RUNE stands.** **Fixed in Ch.15 v2:** the block introduces the F/V pair instead (2→4 and reversed, the last Act 2 pair not yet on the page), no pattern number spoken, matching Ch.13’s “New pattern” phrasing. Ch.16 v1 carries P/B. Act 2 rollout is now complete on the page: 19/21, R and H still owed to Act 3. **One-word consequence for Ch.16 v1**, held, not applied, per author instruction not to touch Ch.16 during the nitpick read: “every reversal since the G” should become “since the V” in the next Ch.16 pass. **Applied 2026-09-03, in Ch.16 v3, same pass as DEF-44 below.** **Lane:** Author ruling on which document was wrong, Claude on the fix. **Closed.**

### DEF-44 — B1.CH16 v2 nitpicks (N1, N2) plus one new find (N3), all fixed in v3 — RESOLVED 2026-09-03

Three items, closed together during Ch.17 drafting and LOAD.

**N1, word-count mislabel plus wrong wording.** Two places in Ch.16 v2 called the query “Four words.” The canonical phrase, locked on the page at Ch.15 (“Is Denic behind.”), is three words. The workshop-scene instance also had Trav recall his own question as “If Denic was behind,” which doesn’t match his own Ch.15 line at all. **Fixed in Ch.16 v3:** both instances now read “Is Denic behind” / “Three words,” matching Ch.15 exactly.

**N2, speaker attribution unclear in two stretches.** The unnamed mek in the workshop aisle (“Is it right you’re getting pulled”) and the Hiopi’s last line in the breakfast exchange with Corw (“There isn’t a third one”) both landed without a dialogue tag, recoverable from context but not stated. **Fixed in Ch.16 v3:** both lines now carry an explicit “she says”/“he says.”

**N3, new find, not part of the original nitpick pair.** Ilyen’s account to Petra has Trav running “the H six more times clean” on Thursday. Thursday’s actual pattern, per Ch.15 v3 as delivered, is F/V, and the six-of-six clean run is specifically the V. **Fixed in Ch.16 v3:** “ran the V six more times clean.”

**Lane:** Claude, mechanical, all three. **Closed.**

### DEF-47 — B1.OUT v8 opened Act Three at Ch.23, contradicting CHIDX and the locked act split — RESOLVED 2026-09-03

Found during the Ch.18 Stage 7 write-back, reading forward to verify DEF-45’s own outstanding flag on Ch.21. B1.OUT v8 carries the header “ACT THREE — Ch. 23-36,” which is fourteen chapters and takes Ch.23 out of Act Two. The act split is LOCKED at 12/11/13/11 across all six books, making Act Two Ch.13-23 and Act Three Ch.24-36, and CHIDX has it right. BUILD Stage 1 is explicit that a chapter number is looked up in CHIDX and never computed from act position, which is the rule this file broke. The same file also labels Ch.22 as the Act Two closer, so it disagreed with itself as well as with CHIDX.

**Fixed in B1.OUT v9, mechanically:** Act Three header moved to Ch.24, Ch.23 restored to Act Two and redated July rather than August. **Not fixed, flagged author-lane inside the outline at the same spot:** Ch.22’s and Ch.23’s content are both currently written as act closers and only one of them can be. Two candidate resolutions written out there, neither taken. **Lane:** Claude on the header, Author on which chapter actually closes the act.

### DEF-46 — B1.OUT Ch.21’s “two months of extra rounds” — RESOLVED 2026-09-03

The line DEF-45 flagged and deliberately left out of scope. Now checkable, since Ch.18 delivered with its own date. Ch.18 is a Friday in mid-May and the habit starts that same evening. Ch.20 opens Curiosity, June. Ch.21 sits after it. That is about five weeks, not two months, the same order of error as DEF-45 and from the same cause, a distance estimated rather than measured against the book’s own openers. **Fixed in B1.OUT v9:** “about five weeks.” **Lane:** Claude, mechanical.

**Worth attaching to both:** three of the last four defects on this queue are the same failure, a span of time asserted in an outline and never checked against a delivered chapter’s own date. The process note added under DEF-42 covers verifying an anchor before trusting distances built on it. This adds the other half, which is that **an outline’s distance figures are estimates until a chapter delivers a date, and should be flagged as estimates in the outline itself rather than written as facts.** B1.OUT v8 did exactly that at Ch.20 and it worked, the flag is what got re-checked and closed. Ch.21 had no flag and survived a pass.

### DEF-45 — B1.OUT v7’s Ch.20 entry claimed “eight weeks” of Ch.18 residue, uncheckable against the book’s own anchors — RESOLVED 2026-09-03

Found during Ch.17 LOAD, neighbour read forward into Ch.20’s outline entry. B1.OUT’s only two hard date anchors in this stretch are Ch.16 (opens the month of Courage, i.e. May, on the page) and Ch.20 (opens Curiosity, i.e. June, same structure). That caps the whole Ch.16-to-Ch.20 span at four to five weeks, and Ch.18 hasn’t even happened yet inside it, so “eight weeks” of residue by Ch.20 was never arithmetically possible on this book’s own calendar. **Fixed in B1.OUT v8:** revised to “closer to three weeks,” with the passage flagged to re-check once Ch.18 is actually drafted with its own date on the page, since this is still an estimate built on two chapter-openers, not a delivered chapter’s own arithmetic. **Not touched, flagged instead:** Ch.21’s nearby “two months of extra rounds” line wasn’t re-verified against the same anchors this pass, scope stayed to the specific line already caught. Worth a look whenever Ch.21 is up. **Followed up 2026-09-03, see DEF-46 above, the line was wrong and is fixed.** The Ch.20 estimate itself is now confirmed against delivered Ch.18 and its re-check flag has come off in B1.OUT v9. **Lane:** Claude, mechanical. **Closed.**

