### DEC-29 — Points economy, gated or ungated — RULED 2026-09-06

v1 of PTS-MATH ended by asking for the call and a v2 carrying it was written and has since been lost. **RULED, author’s own call:** the four path boards (Meeps, Reeps, Tank, Munti, and the power-unit line) are gated behind Year 3 specialisation. The universal genetic and stimulant board is ungated, open from the first week of Year 1, price alone rationing access. Prices are the former ungated column throughout, one column now, not two. **Why this is better than either option v1 offered:** the path gate restores the explanation for the Year 1 cohort looking identical on the field, which ungated pricing had cost, without gating grade, which keeps the locked snowball intact. **Executed 2026-09-06:** PTS-MATH rebuilt as v2 then corrected to v3, Points Shop Catalog regenerated as v2 then repriced as v3, WEAP corrected to v4 on two stale lines, CBT corrected to v5. See DEC-30 for the second half of the ruling. **Lane:** Author, exercised. **Closed.**

### DEF-48 — PTS-MATH v2 lost, rebuilt rather than recovered — OPEN, flagged 2026-09-06

The v2 of Qiraki_Points_Economy_Math is not in the project folder and is not recoverable. It was reported at the time as correcting four defects in v1. Only one of those, the weapon-progression ladder (v1 placed the Heavylance in Y1 Q2 and the Twinlance in Y2, both impossible under the ruling and both contradicting the locked chapter addresses B3.CH24 and B3.CH43), is reconstructible from surviving material and is corrected in the v2 rebuild. **The other three are gone and will surface as new finds if they surface at all.** Same class of loss as Qiraki_Points_Economy_Audit_v1, which v1 names throughout as its companion and which has not been in the folder for at least three sessions. **Kept open rather than closed** because the fix is not known, only the gap. **Lane:** Mixed.

### DEC-30 — Combat days per week, and the path boards priced against the wrong gate — RULED 2026-09-06

Two things, ruled together because the second depends on the first.

**Combat days. RULED:** Friday only in Year 1, Friday and Saturday from Year 2, Thursday to Saturday from Year 3. **This was never actually an open question and that is the finding worth keeping.** CBT has carried “Friday/Saturday only in Years 1-2” as a locked line for some time. PTS-MATH v1 listed the same question as unresolved and nobody read across. CBT’s own version was also wrong, since every delivered Year 1 chapter is Friday-only in narration and dialogue both. Putting Saturday at Year 2 rather than Year 1 leaves Year 1 untouched, which matters because four figures are already on the page: Ch.11’s 2,140 (posted), Ch.21’s 14,640, Corw’s 16,500 and 406, and the whole middle-board scene in Ch.22 which is built on Corw’s 99,000 December projection. Year 2 income goes from 377,400 to 732,600, not to 754,800, since class activity and graded baseline don’t scale with combat days.

**Path prices. RULED, author’s own call to raise them:** the four path boards are rederived against the Year 3 specialisation gate. v1’s ungated column was priced against v1’s grade-by-year mapping, where E belonged to Year 2, and carrying it forward left the first two purchases after specialisation costing a fraction of what a cadet has banked the day the gate opens. New bands in PTS-MATH v3 §5. **The universal board is frozen** at 130, 74,000 and 76,000,000, which are on the page in B1.CH22 and are not movable. The resulting gap between the two columns at E and D is deliberate, has an in-world reason, and per Rule 4 that reason never reaches the page. **Lane:** Author, exercised. **Closed.**

### DEF-49 — Cross-document check never ran between CBT and PTS-MATH — OPEN, flagged 2026-09-06

Root cause behind DEC-30’s first half, logged separately because the fix isn’t a ruling. A locked schedule line sat in CBT while a decision document listed the same question as open, and the delivered chapters contradicted the locked line, three states of the same fact across three files with nothing comparing them. BUILD Stage 2’s load order pulls CBT and PTS separately and never against each other. **Same failure class as the Reqa spelling rule**, which survived on three briefs and in five reference documents while delivered prose quietly contradicted it, and for the same reason: every check verified chapters against a rule instead of the rules against each other. **Fix not chosen:** either Stage 6 gains a cross-document consistency line, or the curriculum documents become the single authority on schedule and PTS stops holding a copy of it. **Lane:** Mixed.

### DEC-31 — Trav’s academy purchase and the hoard payoff — RULED 2026-09-06

**RULED, author’s own call.** One purchase on the page during the academy years, Quickstep at 130 in B1.CH23, and then the hoard spends in one go in the military era. Closes two things that were open: STYLE Rule 14 had never landed on an actual chapter, and CAST’s hoard entry owed a downstream payoff under STYLE §7. **Knock-ons executed the same day:** B1.OUT v10 (Ch.23 gains both purchases, Corw buying on the Saturday between Ch.22 and Ch.23), CAST v23, B3.OUT v5 (Ch.7 retitled Syncline, its old premise assumed the board opened in Year 3 and it does not), B4.OUT v4 (Hotwire price 3,200 to 340,000), Concept v6, Military Era Outline v4. **Lane:** Author, exercised. **Closed.**

### DEC-32 — Six boards, and the power unit is not a path board — RULED 2026-09-06

**RULED:** six boards on the combat-corridor wall, four path boards gated at Year 3 and two narrow ungated ones in the middle, genetic and power unit. **The power unit correction is a defect I introduced and then shipped twice.** Qiraki_Outline_Update_Log has carried the ruling that universal items are the genetic/stimulant line *and* the power unit since neither needs a path to exist, and both Points Shop Catalog v2 and v3 put the power unit behind the Year 3 gate anyway. **Third cross-document miss of the same session and the same class as DEF-49.** The power unit stays priced on the path band regardless of being ungated, which is deliberate: open to a first-year, 400,000 for the cheapest item against a Year 1 income of 111,960, so availability costs nothing and price does the rationing. It also has to stay expensive for Trav’s locked underinvestment to read as a choice. **Lane:** Author for the board count, Claude for the defect. **Closed.**

