### DEC-16 — Orphaned kit reassignment (R-37) — RULED 2026-08-19

New 2026-08-19, from the weekend reconciliation pass (Qiraki_Reconciliation_2026-08-19.docx). Corrected same day, caught during the Military Era Outline sync: this originally only captured Sarah Dufours’s kit, missing Phoebe Asniki’s, which sits on the same open line in Qiraki_Military_Era_Outline_v2.md. Both invented in the lost recovery material, neither exists against tonight’s text, Dufours belongs to Elodie now and Asniki was cut outright.

**RULED, Sarah Dufours’s kit: new character, new slot.** **Naomi Castell**, human, Reeps, extreme long range, fusion lance. Proud of her weapon, nicknamed the **Bloom Eraser**. Cookies and milk as her personal comfort ritual, before or after a mission. Doesn’t rise to Zeteii’s “speed is life” needling, her whole doctrine is never being anywhere the enemy can reach her, and she says so, proudly, which is its own kind of comeback.

**RULED, Phoebe Asniki’s kit: same treatment, second new character.** **Suki Arnesen**, human, Reeps, close-range, slow-firing beam pistol on a rapid-evasion float unit, dances in and out of most weapons’ comfortable range rather than tanking a hit. Physically restless even off the clock, taps a rhythm on her own cockpit rail before every mission, a private countdown the rest of the squad has learned to wait for before moving out. Where Naomi holds still and lets range do the work, Suki never stops moving, a real tactical contrast between the two if they’re ever fielded together.

**Both bench, not yet on either team’s active roster**, both teams already sit full at five pilots. Next up whenever Team One or Team Two actually needs a replacement, rather than forced into an already-locked roster now. Add both to Character Sheets. **Lane:** Author, exercised. **Closed.**

