**2026-08-07:** - **DEF-20, Osnius species description contradiction.** Qiraki_Concept.md’s Osnius entry read “physically near-indistinguishable from human, same basic facial structure,” in direct tension with Qiraki_Character_Sheets.md’s own Bruvald and Peregrine Thale entries, both already written bear-adjacent. Corrected to bear-adjacent at the source, per the author’s direct steer this session, lineage-based coloring (black through brown, grey, white, tied historically to homeworld region, no social weight left in it) added at the same time. See Qiraki_Physical_Description_Bank.md’s change log for exact wording. - **DEF-21, Hiopi body plan implicit rather than stated.** Qiraki_Concept.md already locked Hiopi as quadruped/centaur-built, but Qiraki_Character_Sheets.md’s Vrassik entry, the baseline every other Hiopi character defers to rather than repeats, never actually said so, only “digitigrade legs” and “torso and forearms,” ambiguous enough to read as bipedal. Made explicit in Vrassik’s own entry this session, cross-referenced to Concept.md, not a new decision, just no longer left implicit. - **New file, Qiraki_Physical_Description_Bank.md.** Species-description variance layer and per-character description-variance register, registered in Qiraki_Master_Index.md, Tier 3, ID DESC. **Extended across Books 2-6, same session, new:** every book’s Ch.12 (“The Choice” family) now carries the no-propaganda-opener flag. Second weekend/found-family chapters added by converting an existing, already-“ordinary,” non-propaganda-locked chapter in place, zero renumbering anywhere in the series: Book 2’s Ch.23 “Midpoint” (Trav+Ilyen, post-Wash-Out), Book 3’s Ch.46 “Loose Threads” (Trav+Corw), Book 4’s Ch.46 “Loose Threads” (grief chapter, sits beside Ch.44 Kinship), Book 5’s Ch.46 “Loose Threads” (anger stays undischarged, tightest Rule-4 guardrail in the series, see the chapter’s own note), Book 6’s Ch.46 “Loose Threads” (whole-team ensemble, the found-family throughline’s payoff, callback to B1.CH12’s Yssa beat). Book 5’s own propaganda-allocation note updated to match (~21 chapters on the shared pool now, down from ~23). **Author gave explicit permission to add new chapters to the total where genuinely needed; ended up not needing any**, every second slot was an existing chapter whose own description already matched the job once checked properly, consistent with the merge-before-add discipline holding even when the constraint against it is lifted. - **Weekend-pattern lock, Year 1.** Trav goes home the first two four-day weekends, shifts to staying with Reqa once she confirms she isn’t going home either, a real dip in confidence around month 2 (shown behaviorally, not internally, per his non-reflective hard constraint) gets Yssa to pull him home a third time, and that third trip, dramatized in Ch.12, is what actually locks the staying pattern in for the rest of the book. Written into Qiraki_Book1_Chapter_Outline.md (Ch.10, Ch.12) and both characters’ own CAST entries. Open chapter-count question left inside Ch.12’s own note: whether the Cradle-sponsored event other cadets attend needs its own chapter, author’s call.
